pkgfile
------------------------------------------
pkgfile searches the .files metadata created by repo-add(8) to retrieve file
information about packages. By default, the provided target is considered to be
a filename and pkgfile will return the package(s) which contain this file. The
repos which pkgfile searches is determined by those enabled in
/etc/pacman.conf.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libarchive13-3.8.10-1
  libcurl4-8.23.0-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libintl8-0.22.5-1
  libpcre1-8.45-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libarchive-devel-3.8.10-1
  libcurl-devel-8.23.0-1
  libgmock-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libintl-devel-0.22.5-1
  libpcre-devel-8.45-1
  meson-1.10.2-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/falconindy/pkgfile

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/falconindy/pkgfile/archive/refs/tags/v27.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack pkgfile-27-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./pkgfile-27-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/pkgfile-27-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/pkgfile-27-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

